cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or these analyses, please cite them as below."
title: "negative-steering-analyses: benchmarking negative steering of Boltz-2 on NLR integrated-HMA-domain complexes"
abstract: >-
  The benchmark behind structure-negative-steering, and the analyses that read
  it. Negative steering mutates the receptor surface residues a structure
  prediction wrongly places in contact with its binding partner, so the model
  can no longer settle on that interface. This repository holds the run
  definitions for 18 solved NLR integrated-HMA-domain and MAX-effector
  complexes, a mutation-set dose sweep over the same targets, the
  interface-ablation controls, and nine analysis documents. The engine that
  produced the runs is a submodule, pinned to the commit they were made with.
authors:
